# help environment and help exit-codes print on stdout with exit 0, need no
# config, and still work when config.yaml does not parse.

exec invox help environment
scrubpaths stdout got.txt
cmp got.txt want-environment.txt
! stderr .

exec invox help exit-codes
cmp stdout want-exit-codes.txt
! stderr .

# Extra words after a topic are an unknown topic.
exits 2 invox help exit-codes extra
! stdout .
stderr '^error: unknown help topic "exit-codes extra"$'
exits 2 invox help environment extra
! stdout .
stderr '^error: unknown help topic "environment extra"$'

# A broken config.yaml changes nothing.
mkdir home/.config/invox
cp broken.yaml home/.config/invox/config.yaml
exec invox help environment
scrubpaths stdout got.txt
cmp got.txt want-environment.txt
! stderr .
exec invox help exit-codes
cmp stdout want-exit-codes.txt
! stderr .

-- broken.yaml --
archive:
  dir: [unclosed
-- want-environment.txt --
Environment variables and default directories.

Usage:
  invox help environment

Environment variables:
  INVOX_CONFIG_DIR
      Config directory to use in place of the default one, on every OS. invox
      reads config.yaml and the global support files there, `init` writes there,
      and the legacy directory is not read. It must exist. --config still wins
      for config.yaml.
  XDG_CONFIG_HOME
      Base directory for the config directory, on every OS.
      Default: $HOME/.config. A relative value is ignored.
  XDG_DATA_HOME
      Base directory for the default archive directory on Linux, macOS and other
      Unix systems. Default: $HOME/.local/share, or $HOME/Library/Application
      Support on macOS. Not used on Windows. A relative value is ignored.
  APPDATA
      Base directory for the default archive directory on Windows.
      Default: %USERPROFILE%\AppData\Roaming. Not used elsewhere.
      A relative value is ignored.
  VISUAL
      Editor for `config`, `customer config` and `new -e`. Wins over EDITOR.
  EDITOR
      Editor used when VISUAL is unset. Without either: vi, or notepad on Windows.
  SHELL
      Shell that runs the editor command on macOS, Linux and other Unix systems.
      Default: /bin/sh. On Windows the editor runs through cmd /c.
  INVOX_FORCE_TTY
      Testing aid: any non-empty value makes invox treat stdout as a terminal.

Config directory (config.yaml and the global support files):
  Linux:     $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/invox, else $HOME/.config/invox
  macOS:     $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/invox, else $HOME/.config/invox
  Windows:   %XDG_CONFIG_HOME%\invox, else %USERPROFILE%\.config\invox
  INVOX_CONFIG_DIR replaces it on every OS.
  here:      $WORK/home/.config/invox

Legacy config directory (deprecated):
  invoice-tool next to the invox directory, such as $HOME/.config/invoice-tool.
  A file missing from the invox directory is still read from here, and invox
  prints a warning. `invox init` copies the files into the invox directory.
  Not read when INVOX_CONFIG_DIR is set.

Default archive directory (when config.yaml sets no archive.dir):
  Linux:     $XDG_DATA_HOME/invox/invoices, else $HOME/.local/share/invox/invoices
  macOS:     $XDG_DATA_HOME/invox/invoices, else $HOME/Library/Application Support/invox/invoices
  Windows:   %APPDATA%\invox\invoices, else %USERPROFILE%\AppData\Roaming\invox\invoices
  here:      $DATA_HOME/invox/invoices

Config file:
  1. --config PATH
  2. config.yaml in INVOX_CONFIG_DIR
  3. config.yaml in the config directory
  4. config.yaml in the legacy directory
  A --config file that is missing or broken is an error. invox never falls
  back to another config file.

Precedence:
  An explicit flag wins, then config.yaml, then the defaults above. Environment
  variables only move the default directories; no variable overrides a flag or
  a config.yaml setting.

Support file resolution (customers.yaml, issuer.yaml, invoice_defaults.yaml, template):
  1. explicit flag (-c, -u, -s, -t)
  2. upward search from the current directory
  3. paths.* in config.yaml, relative to config.yaml
  4. the file in the config directory, then in the legacy directory

Upward search:
  It always searches the current directory. It goes up to the nearest directory
  that holds .git, invox.yaml or invoice_defaults.yaml, and stops below your
  home directory, which it searches only when invox runs there. Outside your
  home directory, without such a marker above, it searches only the current
  directory.

Archive directory resolution:
  1. archive.dir in config.yaml, relative to config.yaml
  2. the default archive directory above

Run `invox config paths` to see what each lookup finds.

See also:
  invox help config
-- want-exit-codes.txt --
Exit codes.

Usage:
  invox help exit-codes

Exit codes:
  0    Success.
  1    The command failed: invalid invoice data, a missing or broken file,
       a failed build or a failed external program.
  2    Usage error: unknown command, topic or flag, or a missing or extra
       argument. Also used when a confirmation was declined, or was needed
       without a terminal to ask on and without --yes. The step that needed
       confirmation was not done. Ctrl-C at a confirmation prompt also
       exits 2.
  130  Interrupted by Ctrl-C (SIGINT). Programs invox started are stopped
       and its temporary files are removed.
  143  Stopped by SIGTERM, with the same cleanup as 130.
